<body>
<h1>Purchase Order Reports</h1>
<p>Last updated: 6 Nov 2026</p>
<p>One command, <code>python scripts/po_reports.py &lt;CODE&gt;</code>, exports three purchase order CSV reports for any project, straight from the live database.</p>
<h2>What it does</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Script:</strong> <code>scripts/po_reports.py</code></li>
<li><strong>Data:</strong> active purchase orders only (<code>cancel_status = '0'</code>). Cancelled POs are left out.</li>
<li><strong>Period:</strong> full project history by default. Use <code>--from</code> / <code>--to</code> for a date range.</li>
<li><strong>Output folder:</strong> <code>exports/&lt;Project name&gt;/</code>, for example <code>exports/Sintra/</code>. Running it again overwrites that project's files.</li>
<li><strong>Safety:</strong> it only reads from the database. Nothing in the app or the database is changed.</li>
</ul>
<h2>One-time setup</h2>
<ol>
<li>Check Python 3 is installed: <code>python --version</code></li>
<li>Install the MongoDB driver: <code>pip install pymongo</code></li>
<li>Open a terminal in the project folder: <code>cd D:\Projects\sis-cloud-php</code></li>
</ol>
<p>The database connection is read from <code>include/conn.php</code>, so there is nothing else to configure.</p>
<h2>Commands</h2>
<p>Run these from the project folder. Project codes are not case-sensitive (<code>sn</code> works the same as <code>SN</code>).</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>What you want</th><th>Command</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>See all project codes and PO counts</td><td><code>python scripts/po_reports.py --list</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Full report for one project</td><td><code>python scripts/po_reports.py SN</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Several projects at once</td><td><code>python scripts/po_reports.py AP LX RI</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Every project</td><td><code>python scripts/po_reports.py all</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>A date range</td><td><code>python scripts/po_reports.py FL --from 2025-11-01 --to 2026-10-31</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>From a date up to today</td><td><code>python scripts/po_reports.py IF --from 2026-04-01</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Save to a different folder</td><td><code>python scripts/po_reports.py SN --out D:\Reports\Sintra</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Show help</td><td><code>python scripts/po_reports.py --help</code></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Dates are <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> and are matched on the date the PO was created. Each run prints the PO count, the month range, the grand total and the paths of the files it wrote.</p>
<p>Example output:</p>
<pre><code>&gt; python scripts/po_reports.py SN
SN (S.I.S Sintra): 1307 POs, 4735 items, Mar-2021 to Sep-2025, grand total 138,866,440.72
  D:\Projects\sis-cloud-php\exports\Sintra\Orderlist_SN_complete.csv
  D:\Projects\sis-cloud-php\exports\Sintra\Orderlist_SN_items_complete.csv
  D:\Projects\sis-cloud-php\exports\Sintra\SN_monthwise_quantities_complete.csv</code></pre>
