<h2>Output files</h2>
<p>Each run writes three CSV files per project. <code>&lt;tag&gt;</code> is <code>complete</code> for the full history, or the date range (for example <code>2025-11-01_to_2026-10-31</code>). The files open directly in Excel.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>File</th><th>One row per</th><th>Columns</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>Orderlist_&lt;CODE&gt;_&lt;tag&gt;.csv</code></td><td>PO</td><td>PO_no, PO_Date, Project, Company, Grandtotal, Category</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Orderlist_&lt;CODE&gt;_items_&lt;tag&gt;.csv</code></td><td>PO item, plus transport and plain charge rows</td><td>PO_no, PO_Date, Project, Company, Category, Item_No, HSN_Code, Item, Description, Make, Size, CFT, Qty, Unit, Price, Amount, GST_%, SGST_Amt, CGST_Amt, Item_Total, PO_Grandtotal</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>&lt;CODE&gt;_monthwise_quantities_&lt;tag&gt;.csv</code></td><td>Item and unit</td><td>Category, Item, Unit, one column per month (Mar-2021, Apr-2021 …), Total_Qty, No_of_POs, Total_Value_incl_GST</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<ul>
<li><strong>Summary and items files:</strong> both end with a Total row.</li>
<li><strong>Items file:</strong> PO_Grandtotal is filled only on each PO's first row, so summing that column counts each PO once.</li>
<li><strong>Month-wise file:</strong> every month between the first and last PO gets a column, even months with no purchases. A blank cell means nothing was ordered that month.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How amounts are calculated</h2>
<p>The calculations match the PO PDF (<code>modules/materials/purchase/po_pdf.php</code>), so each PO's rows add up to its grand total.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Row type</th><th>Amount</th><th>Tax</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Standard, Steel, Work, UPVC items</td><td>Qty × Price</td><td>SGST % + CGST % of Amount</td></tr>
<tr><td>Door (timber) items</td><td>CFT × Price (priced per cubic foot)</td><td>SGST % + CGST % of Amount</td></tr>
<tr><td>Transport charges</td><td>trans_amount from the PO</td><td>trans_tax % of Amount, split half SGST, half CGST</td></tr>
<tr><td>Plain charges (Door POs)</td><td>plain_amount × the PO's total CFT</td><td>plain_tax % of Amount, split half SGST, half CGST</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<ul>
<li><strong>Item_Total</strong> = Amount + SGST_Amt + CGST_Amt.</li>
<li><strong>Mismatch check:</strong> if any PO's rows differ from its grand total by more than ₹1, the script prints a WARNING listing those POs.</li>
<li><strong>Month-wise file:</strong> quantities come from item rows only. Transport and plain charges have no quantity, so they are not included there.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Notes and troubleshooting</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>IGST vendors:</strong> tax is always split into SGST and CGST, as stored in the database. The PO PDF shows the same tax as IGST for these vendors, so add the two columns together.</li>
<li><strong>Item names are free text.</strong> The same material typed differently on different POs (for example "M Fold Tissue" and "M-Fold Tissue") shows as separate rows in the month-wise file. Rows are merged only when the name and unit match, ignoring capitalisation and spacing.</li>
<li><strong>Ordered, not received.</strong> Quantities are what was ordered on POs, not what was received at site.</li>
<li><strong>Months come from the PO date</strong> (<code>po_date</code>). The <code>--from</code> / <code>--to</code> filter uses the PO creation time (<code>date_time</code>), which is normally the same day.</li>
<li><strong>Files open in Excel?</strong> Close a CSV in Excel before re-running, or the script can't overwrite it (PermissionError).</li>
<li><code>ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pymongo'</code> → run <code>pip install pymongo</code>.</li>
<li><code>unknown project code</code> → check the code with <code>python scripts/po_reports.py --list</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Connection timeout</strong> → check the internet connection; the database servers are remote.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Updating this document</h2>
<p>Edit <code>docs/PO_REPORTS.md</code>, then regenerate the HTML and Word versions:</p>
<pre><code>cd docs
node _md2html.js PO_REPORTS.md</code></pre>

</body></html>